{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2155-12-19 17:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I understand you had sudden pain in your transplanted kidney earlier today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2155-12-19 17:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it started in my lower right side and spread across my belly and up into my chest. I was sweating and it didn’t go away for almost an hour."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2155-12-19 17:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. That sounds very uncomfortable. The good news is the pain went away before you got here?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2155-12-19 17:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it suddenly stopped on the way in the ambulance. I feel okay now, just worried."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2155-12-19 17:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s reassuring. We’re going to run some tests, including an ultrasound of your transplanted kidney, to see if there’s any blockage or other issue."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2155-12-19 17:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I’ve been tracking my urine output. It’s less than before, but total is around 1100 mL a day between the tube and voiding."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2155-12-19 17:37:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s helpful. We’ll monitor that closely. Any fever, nausea, or chills?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2155-12-19 17:38:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, none of that. But I’ve had loose greenish stools since starting linezolid for the VRE infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2155-12-19 17:39:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a known side effect. We’ll keep an eye on it. Let’s get the ultrasound done and go from there."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2155-12-19 19:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The ultrasound is back. There’s still hydronephrosis in the transplanted kidney. The nephrostomy tube is in a calyx but not clearly in the renal pelvis, so it might not be draining well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2155-12-19 19:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So the tube isn’t working right? Could that be why I had pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2155-12-19 19:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. The blockage may have caused pressure to build up. We’re scheduling a nephrostogram tomorrow to check the tube and possibly place a stent."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2155-12-19 19:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A stent? What does that do?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2155-12-19 19:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s a small tube that goes from the kidney to the bladder, bypassing the blockage. It should help drain urine properly and prevent future pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2155-12-19 19:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. Will I be awake for it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2155-12-19 19:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll get light sedation, so you’ll be relaxed but not fully asleep. The radiologist will guide everything with imaging."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2155-12-20 11:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re about to start the nephrostogram. The team will check the current tube and place a stent if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2155-12-20 11:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’m ready. Just let me know what’s happening."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2155-12-20 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news — the procedure went well. We confirmed the nephrostomy tube had pulled back, and there was a blockage in the upper ureter. We placed an 8 Fr x 10 cm stent across it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2155-12-20 13:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So the blockage is fixed? Does that mean I’m better?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2155-12-20 13:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The stent should relieve the obstruction. Your creatinine was 2.9 on admission — we’ll watch it closely to see if it improves."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2155-12-21 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your creatinine is down to 2.6 today — that’s a good sign the kidney is draining better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2155-12-21 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. But I’ve been feeling some jaw and shoulder pain, and burning in my chest, especially when I lie down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2155-12-21 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We checked your cardiac enzymes four times — all negative. EKG shows your usual atrial fibrillation, but no signs of heart attack."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2155-12-21 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not my heart?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2155-12-21 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Unlikely. The pain improving when you sit up suggests reflux. We’ve consulted GI. They recommend continuing omeprazole and nystatin for thrush."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2155-12-21 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been on omeprazole before. Should I take more?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2155-12-21 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re increasing it to 40 mg twice daily. We may do an endoscopy later to check for esophagitis, but your symptoms are improving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2155-12-22 07:50:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your creatinine is now 2.5. Still not where we want it, so we’re planning a kidney biopsy tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2155-12-22 07:51:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Another procedure? Is something wrong?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2155-12-22 07:52:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s to check if there’s rejection or other damage. Since your creatinine isn’t dropping fast, we want to be sure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2155-12-22 07:53:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I trust you. Do I need to stop any meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2155-12-22 07:54:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re already off Coumadin, which helps. The biopsy is low risk, and we’ll do it with ultrasound guidance."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2155-12-24 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The biopsy is done. No signs of rejection, which is excellent. But we did see donor disease, which means the kidney had some pre-existing changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2155-12-24 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not rejection, but the kidney wasn’t perfect to start with?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2155-12-24 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. That explains why recovery is slower. The stent should help, and we’ll keep supporting kidney function."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2155-12-25 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We tried capping your nephrostomy tube yesterday, but you had low urine output and a burning sensation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2155-12-25 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, only 50 cc when I tried to void. Then 120 cc came out when you uncapped the tube."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2155-12-25 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We think you were dehydrated — you were NPO for the possible endoscopy. We gave fluids, and your output improved."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2155-12-25 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I need to stay hydrated?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2155-12-25 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Very important. We’ll keep the tube open for now and reassess as an outpatient."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2155-12-25 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. What about my Coumadin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2155-12-25 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We restarted it yesterday. Your INR will be checked soon, and your PCP will manage it going forward."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2155-12-26 07:50:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs are stable. Creatinine is 2.4 — best we’ve seen. We’re planning to discharge you tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2155-12-26 07:51:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What do I need to do at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2155-12-26 07:52:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Keep the nephrostomy tube open to gravity drainage and record output daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2155-12-26 07:53:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And if something seems wrong?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2155-12-26 07:54:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call the transplant office if you have fever, chills, pain, redness, or decreased output. Also, keep taking linezolid for the full 10 days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2155-12-26 07:55:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. What about the green stools?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2155-12-26 07:56:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Should improve after you finish the antibiotic. Stay hydrated and eat small, frequent meals."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2155-12-26 07:57:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my heartburn?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2155-12-26 07:58:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Continue omeprazole twice daily and nystatin for thrush. Follow up with GI in two weeks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2155-12-26 07:59:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. Any other tests before I go?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2155-12-26 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We checked G6PD today because of your allergy to Bactrim. It’ll help us choose the right infection prevention med."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2155-12-26 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember — I had palpitations with pentamidine before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2155-12-26 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Right, so we’re being careful. We’ll decide on dapsone or another option based on the result."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2155-12-27 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All set for discharge. Your condition is stable, and you’re feeling well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2155-12-27 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I’ll follow all the instructions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2155-12-27 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last thing — get your labs drawn as scheduled and follow up with your transplant team."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2155-12-27 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I’m just glad the pain’s gone and the kidney is working better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2155-12-27 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re glad too. Take care, and don’t hesitate to call if anything comes up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2155-12-27 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2155-12-27 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You're welcome. Have a safe trip home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2155-12-27 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. See you at the follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2155-12-27 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll see you then. Rest well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2155-12-27 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I plan to. Thank you for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2155-12-27 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You're doing great. Just keep up with the care plan."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 68,
      "time": "2155-12-27 09:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I’ve learned a lot this time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 69,
      "time": "2155-12-27 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s the best outcome — staying informed and healthy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 70,
      "time": "2155-12-27 09:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel ready to go home now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 71,
      "time": "2155-12-27 09:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re ready to send you off. Take it easy and call if you need anything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 72,
      "time": "2155-12-27 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 73,
      "time": "2155-12-27 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You're very welcome. Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 74,
      "time": "2155-12-27 09:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. See you soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 75,
      "time": "2155-12-27 09:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. We’ll be here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 76,
      "time": "2155-12-27 09:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks. I feel safe knowing that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 77,
      "time": "2155-12-27 09:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s what we’re here for. Have a good day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 78,
      "time": "2155-12-27 09:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "You too, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 79,
      "time": "2155-12-27 09:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take it easy at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 80,
      "time": "2155-12-27 09:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. No rushing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 81,
      "time": "2155-12-27 09:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. That’s the best medicine right now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 82,
      "time": "2155-12-27 09:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I agree. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 83,
      "time": "2155-12-27 09:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You're welcome. We’ll see you soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 84,
      "time": "2155-12-27 09:27:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Looking forward to it. Bye for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 85,
      "time": "2155-12-27 09:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Goodbye. Take care."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2155-12-19 17:31:00",
    "admission_end": "2155-12-27 14:43:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted with sudden-onset pain near her transplanted kidney, found to be due to persistent hydronephrosis despite a nephrostomy tube, which imaging showed was malpositioned. A nephrostogram confirmed ureteral obstruction, and a stent was successfully placed. Creatinine improved from 2.9 to 2.4 mg/dL. A kidney biopsy ruled out rejection but showed donor disease. The patient developed transient epigastric and referred pain, but cardiac workup was negative; symptoms were attributed to reflux, managed with omeprazole. Oral thrush was treated with nystatin. The nephrostomy tube was kept open due to low urine output when capped, likely from dehydration. She was discharged home stable, with instructions to continue linezolid, keep the tube open, monitor output, and follow up for labs and GI evaluation.",
    "problems": [
      "Complications of transplanted kidney",
      "Acute kidney failure, unspecified",
      "Other ureteric obstruction",
      "Urinary tract infection, site not specified",
      "Candidiasis of mouth",
      "Hydronephrosis",
      "Surgical operation with transplant of whole organ causing abnormal patient reaction, or later complication, without mention of misadventure at time of operation",
      "Urinary complications, not elsewhere classified",
      "Surgical operation with implant of artificial internal device causing abnormal patient reaction, or later complication,without mention of misadventure at time of operation",
      "Urethral stricture, unspecified",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Atrial fibrillation",
      "Long-term (current) use of anticoagulants",
      "Mitral valve disorders",
      "Postsurgical hypothyroidism",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Tricuspid valve disorders, specified as nonrheumatic",
      "Primary hyperparathyroidism",
      "Dehydration"
    ]
  }
}
